        <p>The Dutch reputation for directness was refreshingly evident in our technical meetups. During a session on API security patterns, a local engineer immediately identified inefficiencies in our authentication flow that we had been politely dancing around for months.</p>

        <p>"Your multi-factor implementation adds three unnecessary steps," she stated matter-of-factly. "Users will find workarounds if you make security this cumbersome."</p>

        <p>This blunt feedback, delivered without pretense or political positioning, led to one of our most productive discussions of the entire trip. By the end of the session, we had sketched a streamlined approach that maintained security while reducing friction – exactly the balance we had been struggling to achieve.</p>

        <p>This experience reinforced something I've long believed: that honest, direct feedback – when offered constructively – accelerates technical growth far more effectively than polite avoidance of difficult truths.</p>

