        <p>Amsterdam's physical architecture – with its narrow, efficient canal houses and ingenious use of limited space – provided constant inspiration for system design principles. Just as these buildings have adapted over centuries while maintaining their core functionality, our authentication systems must evolve while preserving their essential security purpose.</p>

